  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Opened by the city of Fréjus and presented by the tourist office on 24 March 2025, Woof &amp; Wow is a fully fenced dog park set in the heart of the Base Nature François Léotard, along the access to the events car park. On a large landscaped area, dogs can run, sniff and socialise freely, under their owner's supervision. An agility course with natural obstacles (driftwood trunks, tunnel, etc.) adds variety to the games.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The rules announced by the city are simple: access is strictly forbidden to category 1 and 2 dogs, owners remain responsible for their animal and must pick up waste immediately (€135 fine for non-compliance, article R634-2 of the Criminal Code), and constant supervision of the dog is required.</p>
      <p>As for facilities, the fence is reinforced against escapes, three secure gates are provided for pedestrians and a wide gate for service vehicles. A push tap lets your dog drink on site. Neither the city's page nor the tourist office's gives hours specific to the park; the Base Nature itself is open every day from 7:30am to 11pm (midnight in July and August) and access is free.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: keep an eye on your dog at all times and pick up straight away, it's the city's rule.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Base Nature François Léotard covers 135 hectares by the sea, of which 80 to 85 are protected natural areas according to the city and tourist office pages, and has a large free car park. The Base Nature reception answers on 04 94 51 91 10. For the beach, the Fréjus tourist office publishes a "Plages pour les chiens" page to read before you leave, as the rules vary by beach and season.</p>
    </div>

